Sir,

You have raised me from a gentlewoman to a marchioness, from a marchioness to=
 a queen. There remains only to raise me, as you intend, to be a saint in hea=
ven.

I ask only an open trial, and that my honour be not buried with me. Whatever =
becomes of me, our daughter is innocent of all.

From my cheerless lodging in the Tower,
Anne
